# FocusProLab core

Before non-trivial work, read `docs/CLAUDE-HANDOFF.md` and `AGENTS.md`.

## Product facts

- SPA: Vite + React; backend Supabase; deploy Vercel from `main`.
- User-facing scores and PDFs use **V4** (`ACTIVE_REPORT_SCORING_VERSION` in `src/scoringVersion.js`). V1–V3 remain for research/compare only.
- Four indices: **A** attention (omissions), **T** timing (stability + late; mean RT speed not scored in V3/V4), **I** impulsivity (false alarms), **H** motor (multi + idle only).

## Never without explicit human approval

- Turning on any flag in `src/testQaMode.js` for a production deploy.
- Changing V4 T/overall weights or reintroducing mean-RT speed into T.
- Forcing overall included-RT N to equal sum of phase included-RT N (per-slice IQR is intentional; audit rule B).
- Adding another `complete_test_session` RPC overload signature.
- Emailing admin press-timeline PDFs to clients.

## Change hygiene

- Prefer the intervention table in `docs/CLAUDE-HANDOFF.md` §10 over hunting randomly.
- Match existing patterns; keep TR/EN/IT PDF strings in sync when editing report copy.
- Practice (`practiceRun`) must not persist sessions.
- After score or PDF-copy changes that affect Storage attachments, plan a report refresh.
